# Project Context Embeddings Integration

Integrate project context embeddings into the Void editor using the local proxy's `/v1/embeddings` endpoint. This will enable semantic search and enhance the existing "functional semantic graph" for better code context.

## Proposed Changes

### Common Layer

#### [MODIFY] [sendLLMMessageTypes.ts](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/common/sendLLMMessageTypes.ts)
- Add [EmbeddingsParams](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/common/sendLLMMessageTypes.ts#220-227) and `EmbeddingsResponse` types for IPC-based embedding requests.
- Add [MainEmbeddingsParams](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/common/sendLLMMessageTypes.ts#236-237) and [EventEmbeddingsOnSuccessParams](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/common/sendLLMMessageTypes.ts#238-239) for IPC event handling.

#### [MODIFY] [sendLLMMessageService.ts](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/common/sendLLMMessageService.ts)
- Add [getEmbeddings](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/electron-main/llmMessage/sendLLMMessage.impl.ts#984-985) method to [ILLMMessageService](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/common/sendLLMMessageService.ts#21-29) to bridge the frontend and backend for embedding requests.

---

### Electron-Main Layer

#### [MODIFY] [sendLLMMessageChannel.ts](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/electron-main/sendLLMMessageChannel.ts)
- Add [getEmbeddings](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/electron-main/llmMessage/sendLLMMessage.impl.ts#984-985) command to the IPC channel to handle requests from the browser.
- Emit `onSuccess_embeddings` and `onError_embeddings` events back to the browser.

#### [MODIFY] [sendLLMMessage.impl.ts](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/electron-main/llmMessage/sendLLMMessage.impl.ts)
- Implement [_sendOpenAICompatibleEmbeddings](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/electron-main/llmMessage/sendLLMMessage.impl.ts#429-447) to call the local proxy's `/v1/embeddings` endpoint.
- Register this implementation in `sendLLMMessageToProviderImplementation`.

---

### Browser Layer

#### [NEW] [voidEmbeddingProvider.ts](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/browser/voidEmbeddingProvider.ts)
- Implement [IAiEmbeddingVectorProvider](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/services/aiEmbeddingVector/common/aiEmbeddingVectorService.ts#25-28) using the `ILLMMessageService.getEmbeddings` method.
- Register the provider with VS Code's [IAiEmbeddingVectorService](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/services/aiEmbeddingVector/common/aiEmbeddingVectorService.ts#16-24).

#### [MODIFY] [contextGatheringService.ts](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/src/vs/workbench/contrib/void/browser/contextGatheringService.ts)
- Integrate semantic retrieval using the embedding provider to supplement the existing graph-based context.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Verify embedding retrieval via a script that calls `ILLMMessageService.getEmbeddings`.
- Test IPC communication by triggering an embedding request from the developer console.

### Manual Verification
- Check that the local proxy logs record requests to `/v1/embeddings` when the chat mode is set to "gather".
- Verify that semantic context (Snippets) are included in the LLM prompt.

## Observability & Verification

To ensure the system is working, I will add prominent logging:
- **Embedding Heartbeat**: Log "Void: Creating embedding for [text...]" in `VoidEmbeddingProvider.ts`.
- **Semantic Search Heartbeat**: Log "Void: Performing semantic search for: [query]" and "Void: Found [N] snippets" in `ContextGatheringService.ts`.

These logs will be visible in:
1. The **terminal** where you run [./scripts/code.sh](file:///home/shivam/Desktop/Shivam/void/scripts/code.sh).
2. The **Developer Tools Console** (Help -> Toggle Developer Tools).
